# Backend conventions

- Services in `backend/app/*.py`; routes in `api.py` with `require_permission`
- Models in `models.py`; Pydantic schemas in `schemas.py`
- New tables/columns → Alembic revision under `backend/alembic/versions/`
- Async SQLAlchemy sessions; always filter by `tenant_id` on tenant-owned rows
- Side effects (stock, ledger, tax, credit, audit) must stay transactionally correct
- Tests in `backend/tests/`; prefer Docker pytest command used in the repo

```python
# ❌ BAD — success without doing the work
return env({"ok": True}, "Backup completed")

# ✅ GOOD — only return success after real work + commit
await backup_svc.run(...)
await db.commit()
return env(serialize(job), "Backup completed")
```
